father said: don't put all your trust in
your brothers,

232
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:23,700
"lest they plot against you. Indeed Satan
is to man a clear enemy."

233
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:27,660
This brotherhood… through Satan. Satan
says: "Say

234
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:31,420
to My servants that which is best." Why,
Lord, must

235
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:34,800
I say the best word? The final

236
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:38,220
word I'd love to say it, but

237
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:41,740
I choose the best. Why? To close

238
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:46,340
the door: "Indeed Satan sows discord
between them." Satan comes

239
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:51,260
of that word; it may land on the dryness
of his heart and ignite.

240
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:56,020
Satan lives in the word. Imagine the
Companions

241
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,020
passing by and finding the Prophet ﷺ with

242
00:15:58,040 --> 00:16:01,620
his wife Safiyyah at night. They hurried
away,

243
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:05,260
so he said: take it easy, slow down —

244
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:10,980
it's Safiyyah, my wife! They said: Glory to Allah,
O Messenger of Allah — do you doubt us,

245
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,980
or do we doubt you? He said: no, I don't
doubt you, but Satan

246
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:20,300
runs through the son of Adam like blood.
You can't control that.

247
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:24,940
When we keep Satan's enmity present, seek
refuge from him, and know that the first

248
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:28,820
driver — revenge — is Satan's driver, a
person starts…

249
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:32,420
to use his mind. He judges a lot,
remembers Allah,

250
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:36,980
keeps his remembrance, and feels his
battles

251
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,980
with Satan. Every moment is a battle:
entering, eating, sleeping.

252
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:44,820
Sleep: he ties a knot at your ear and
urinates in it,

253
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,180
ties at your head and urinates in your
nostril. Has it come to this…

254
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:51,780
and on your way to the mosque he meets
you, and inside the

255
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:55,420
mosque between you and the people —
present in every

256
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:57,260
detail of our life. So how do we make him
absent from

257
00:16:57,280 --> 00:17:01,820
our educational discourse, and from our
talk about human

258
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:05,330
relationships and the like? … treating him
as something marginal.

259
00:17:06,930 --> 00:17:10,280
This system… it becomes like a car.

260
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:15,320
can you guarantee the trip is good? No.
One: the destination is Allah.

261
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:20,200
The map? The Hereafter. That's the
Hereafter… and riding with you

262
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:25,000
is the other person. The driver? Your own
self.

263
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:29,040
Is it good? It is. Trustworthy? It is. A
driver? A committed driver

264
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:32,400
to the rules… committed to the rules. Then
there are road signs.

265
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:37,360
Those road signs are Satan's signs:

266
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:41,960
here, from here it's better." He offers
excitement,

267
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:44,800
but you were raised on the higher path, so
you don't go.

268
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:48,960
"Money — but through crooked ways." You
say: no, I want blessing.

269
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:53,200
So you adjust your course according to the
destination

270
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:56,720
and the map. Now, who

271
00:17:56,760 --> 00:18:00,280
will confuse you? The other,

272
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:04,640
he says: turn, turn, turn — just turn,
let's try it,

273
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:09,160
and he drags you off course. Or the second
one,

274
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:14,520
the one actually driving beside you,
pulling you toward

275
00:18:14,540 --> 00:18:17,560
a place you never wanted to reach. So
we're talking about

276
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:22,800
who rides with you, who sets your
direction, where you're going. All of this

277
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:26,440
helps me keep my relationship with others
in order. First:

278
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:32,040
the relationship with Allah, glory be to
Him. Okay,

279
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:36,160
on making Allah one. We have two ropes:

280
00:18:36,180 --> 00:18:40,200
a rope rising from below to above — that's
prayer; a person holds

281
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:43,840
on to prayer — and a rope coming down,
which is the Qur'an.

282
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:47,880
You hold both, and you're connected to the
sky.

283
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:52,440
The relationship with Allah affects a
person's relationship with

284
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:57,680
himself, with others, with the world, and
it resets everything,

285
00:18:57,700 --> 00:19:01,360
because it is a relationship with Allah.
So how does the relationship

286
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:05,920
with Allah reset the rest? One:

287
00:19:05,940 --> 00:19:11,080
who entered the Fire because of a cat.
Meaning: a relationship

288
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:14,440
with a cat ruined her relationship with
Allah,

289
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:17,920
and another woman entered Paradise because
of a dog she gave water to!

290
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:22,480
My Lord… Paradise and Fire?! For this,
souls are

291
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:28,720
punished, necks and heads bowed in dust?
My Lord,

292
00:19:28,740 --> 00:19:32,760
because they pleased Allah, glory be to
Him;

293
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:37,760
they knew the relationship with Allah,

294
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:41,800
because they did it for Allah's sake.

295
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:46,120
they said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so
died. He said: she is in

296
00:19:46,140 --> 00:19:51,720
the Fire. They said: she fasted and prayed
all night!

297
00:19:51,740 --> 00:19:53,960
She fasted and prayed! He said: she is in
the Fire. They said: O

298
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:59,040
Messenger of Allah?! He said: she harmed
her neighbours with her tongue.

299
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:02,480
How can relationships and dealings ruin

300
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:05,960
your acts of worship? True.

301
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:12,080
is bankrupt? They said: the bankrupt among
us is the one with no dirham

302
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:16,000
of Resurrection with his prayer, zakat and
fasting, but he

303
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:19,960
stole this one's wealth, hit this one,
insulted this one.

304
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:25,120
Dealings, dealings, dealings. Look:
worship,

305
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:31,120
worship, worship, and dealings, dealings,
dealings.

306
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:36,160
against their wrongs; when their good
deeds run out, He takes from their sins

307
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:39,040
and places them on his scale, then he is
thrown on his face into

308
00:20:39,060 --> 00:20:42,160
the Fire. We speak about worship, but
dealings

309
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:45,520
eroded it heavily. The relationship with
Allah — the more

310
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:50,600
a person's relationship with his Lord is

311
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:54,000
excellent, the more it reflects on
himself, and reflects on

312
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:56,640
his relationships with others. When we
talk

313
00:20:56,660 --> 00:21:00,520
about a person's relationship with Allah…
and the relationship

314
00:21:00,540 --> 00:21:04,640
— the relationship with Allah isn't in
front of people.

315
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:09,720
Real success is what is hidden from
people, not what appears to them.

316
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:12,920
That's why: the secret of success is
succeeding in secret.

317
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:16,480
The secret of success is succeeding in
secret.

318
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:20,160
And what is piety? They asked an old man:
what is piety? He said:

319
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:23,080
how are you when you're alone? When you're
alone,

320
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:26,080
not in front of people, not in the age of
appearances…

321
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:29,400
How are you when

322
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:32,760
you're alone? When you are

323
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:36,480
by yourself in private, how is your
relationship with Allah,

324
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,840
glory be to Him? Because that itself
affects your relationship

325
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:42,960
with yourself, your relationships with
others, your understanding of life,

326
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:45,830
and your inner resilience, and more.

327
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:53,420
When I see the real you, and you see the
real me,

328
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:56,060
the situation becomes far more sensitive.
You might not

329
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:58,500
accept it from me. So let's talk about

330
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:04,220
speaking plainly and criticism. At the
start — what do you think?

331
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:09,100
Okay. Again, let's separate: we
distinguish

332
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:13,380
between the concept and the strategies. I
can give you strategies for receiving criticism,

333
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:18,580
how to say it, the sandwich method…
whatever.

334
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:27,300
criticism itself. First: distinguish
opinion from fact.

335
00:22:27,340 --> 00:22:31,420
You tell me: "By Allah, Abu Abdulrahman,
your prayer beads didn't appeal to me" —

336
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:35,700
that's an opinion. "I don't like your
style": opinion. "I don't like how you look":

337
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:40,300
opinion. Deal with opinions like a garment

338
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:43,620
that fits you — or take it off. But a
fact? No — benefit

339
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:46,220
from it. A fact is a fact. Like: you came
to me

340
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:48,980
late; two days ago you came late, and you

341
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:52,980
promised and didn't do it. These are facts
you must take

342
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:58,420
into account in others' criticism of you.
Now,

343
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:01,380
when does an opinion rise to the level of
fact? When it's frequent.

344
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:06,460
When more than one person comes with the
same opinion… then

345
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:09,860
I raise it to the level of fact. I must…
must

346
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:15,140
pay attention. Another point: the very
word "criticism

347
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:19,580
of others" — critique is taken from the
money-changer, from

348
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:22,920
from the genuine, the adulterated from the

349
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:26,300
sound. A critic. So criticism does not

350
00:23:26,340 --> 00:23:30,180
mean insult. Criticism means: pros, cons —
sort this

351
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:33,300
and sort that; that's the critic. Now,
concepts about

352
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:39,460
criticism: the first mistake is that I
must please

353
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:44,820
everyone, in everything, all the time —
and I can't, I can't.

354
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:48,160
such a great, awe-inspiring imam — says

355
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:51,540
to Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, his cousin, one

356
00:23:51,580 --> 00:23:56,340
of his students: what do people say about
me?

357
00:23:56,360 --> 00:24:00,940
"What do people say about me?" He said:
some praise, some criticise

358
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:03,940
Anas ibn Malik — both praise and
criticism.

359
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:07,420
He said: what did he say? He said
something amazing: people are still

360
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:13,500
between a praiser and a criticiser. That's
normal. But we seek refuge in Allah from

361
00:24:13,520 --> 00:24:19,420
We seek refuge in Allah from that… it
becomes a fact.

362
00:24:19,440 --> 00:24:24,540
Yes, that's a real problem. Now, do
people's words matter?

363
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:30,220
his supplication said: O Allah, I seek
refuge in You from the hardship

364
00:24:30,240 --> 00:24:33,440
of affliction, being overtaken by misery,
and

365
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:36,700
the gloating of enemies. He sought refuge

366
00:24:36,740 --> 00:24:40,340
from it… and what about people's words:
"We already know that your chest

367
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:45,540
tightens because of what they say." The
Prophet's chest ﷺ

368
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:48,140
tightened over this matter. People's words
— a wise person takes them into account,

369
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:52,020
takes them into account, they don't break
him, but he takes them

370
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:55,940
into account and guards against them. They
said:

371
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:58,940
blessed is the one who wards off
backbiting from himself. Meaning:

372
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:02,620
not exposing yourself, not: I'll do
whatever I want and ignore what

373
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:06,780
people say. No. Umar, may Allah be pleased
with him, said: whoever places himself in

374
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:10,620
a position of suspicion should not blame
those who think badly of him.

375
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:16,500
Brother, don't say… don't think you're
above

376
00:25:16,520 --> 00:25:21,860
mistakes or above others' criticism. Let
me give…

377
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:25,580
kills his companions… "Do not put me to
shame regarding

378
00:25:25,620 --> 00:25:29,340
my guest"; is there no sensible man among
you?

379
00:25:29,380 --> 00:25:33,700
What do people say? Criticism… yes, it can
matter for

380
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:36,260
refining ourselves; we take what's right,
but it doesn't break us, it doesn't

381
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:41,220
steer us, it isn't the compass. It isn't
the compass?

382
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:44,260
Good. Two or three. One of the most

383
00:25:44,280 --> 00:25:48,100
important things: that lad who studied
with his uncle.

384
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:51,300
His uncle was an imam among the imams of
the Muslims,

385
00:25:51,320 --> 00:25:54,820
and he said to him — a man learned in
students

386
00:25:54,840 --> 00:26:00,140
and seekers of knowledge — he said: my
son, by Allah,

387
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:03,500
you are no good for this! Every day you
study,

388
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:08,660
your mental capacity is weak. It broke his
heart…

389
00:26:08,680 --> 00:26:11,820
The student says: I understood. I left
with it in my face,

390
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:14,060
and sought knowledge. He says: until
people gathered around me.

391
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:19,220
Wonderful! He began to teach… he became a
teacher.

392
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:23,140
He says: when people gathered around me
and I looked

393
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:25,380
at them, I said: may Allah have mercy on
my uncle… he didn't lie; if

394
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:28,460
he were alive, he would have paid the
expiation for his oath.

395
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:32,880
Because he swore: "you are no good." Who
is

396
00:26:32,920 --> 00:26:36,340
this boy? This lad is the great imam —
